```
id: SPL-021
name: Activity from TOR exit nodes
description: Sign-in or perimeter events whose source address matches the TOR exit node lookup.
platform: Splunk
mitre_tactic: Command and Control
mitre_technique: T1090.003 Proxy: Multi-hop Proxy
severity: Medium
data_source: index=azure; index=firewall; lookup tor_exit_nodes
false_positives: Privacy-conscious users; stale lookup entries.
tuning: Refresh the lookup daily from a threat intelligence feed.
test_method: Connect through the TOR browser after adding a live exit node to the lookup.
owner: <OWNER>
status: Draft
last_review: 2026-11-19
```
(index=azure sourcetype="mscs:azure:eventhub" category=SignInLogs) OR (index=firewall) earliest=-1d
| eval src_ip=coalesce('properties.ipAddress', src)
| lookup tor_exit_nodes ip AS src_ip OUTPUT is_tor
| where is_tor="true"
| stats count values(index) AS sources values(properties.userPrincipalName) AS users BY src_ip
| sort - count
